{"w":2400,"h":3395,"lines":[{"t":"Audioscripts","x":0.12754086691314573,"w":0.11323102315266928,"h":0.014778896551952192,"c":1,"y":0.10016869124431615},{"c":1,"t":"Right, well the eucalyptus tree is an important tree for lots of reasons. For example, it gives","x":0.13163208201712753,"w":0.67501378377278654,"y":0.14152720830162613,"h":0.014503452044914877},{"t":"shelter to creatures like birds and bats, and these and other species also depend on it for","y":0.1569493520564248,"w":0.66255142211914064,"h":0.011778563015312105,"x":0.13168725197496181,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.16915455797195689,"h":0.017123596407078279,"x":0.12954333920455383,"w":0.64423207600911458,"t":"food, particularly the nectar from its flowers. So it supports biodiversity. It's useful to us"},{"w":0.65035171508789058,"h":0.01561903981634527,"c":1,"x":0.13161741899899312,"y":0.1844700611380452,"t":"humans too, because we can kill germs with a disinfectant made from oil extracted from"},{"h":0.011778563015312216,"t":"eucalyptus leaves.","x":0.13168724517216934,"y":0.20200235571472747,"w":0.13991769154866535,"c":1},{"x":0.13163995303593728,"w":0.67498550415039071,"t":"The eucalyptus grows all over Australia and the trees can live for up to four hundred years.","h":0.014871494508884919,"y":0.22095396181449733,"c":1},{"y":0.2356352082234654,"x":0.13161503121144183,"c":1,"t":"So it's alarming that all across the country, numbers of eucalyptus are falling because the","h":0.015665137444845545,"w":0.66270797729492192},{"y":0.24858010871223513,"h":0.016851289252650781,"c":1,"t":"trees are dying off prematurely. So what are the reasons for this?","x":0.13153905438976612,"w":0.48179290771484373},{"w":0.68528010050455723,"c":1,"t":"One possible reason is disease. As far back as the 1970s the trees started getting a disease","y":0.27153146493762925,"h":0.014915088882715866,"x":0.13164305629048451},{"t":"called Mundulla Yellows. The trees' leaves would gradually turn yellow, then the tree would","w":0.6729667154947917,"x":0.13162287592299929,"y":0.28597897745002743,"c":1,"h":0.015014738300804353},{"y":0.30087209324932451,"w":0.63374481201171884,"h":0.013081394460653373,"x":0.13168727136039554,"t":"die. It wasn't until 2004 that they found the cause of the problem was lime, or calcium","c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.13162229198219128,"t":"hydroxide to give it its proper chemical name, which was being used in the construction","y":0.31494033090079621,"w":0.64827529907226555,"h":0.015048139367704549},{"c":1,"w":0.65637858072916666,"h":0.013250883392226132,"y":0.32979976455306581,"t":"of roads. The lime was being washed away into the ground and affecting the roots of the","x":0.1316872529432277},{"h":0.01453488398216074,"t":"eucalyptus trees nearby. What it was doing was preventing the trees from sucking up the iron","x":0.12962963399158278,"y":0.34447674405166573,"c":1,"w":0.69341562906901044},{"c":1,"t":"they needed for healthy growth. When this was injected back into the affected trees, they","y":0.35895170804211052,"w":0.66255142211914064,"x":0.12962963879675157,"h":0.014723203769140158},{"h":0.011631330977620591,"t":"immediately recovered.","x":0.12962962763918393,"y":0.3749999998884177,"w":0.17901234944661457,"c":1},{"x":0.13168724370615356,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722,"w":0.66049382527669265,"y":0.395348837088074,"t":"But this problem only affected a relatively small number of trees. By 2000, huge numbers"},{"w":0.65860682169596352,"y":0.40828501877212631,"h":0.01555202425719715,"t":"of eucalyptus were dying along Australia's East Coast, of a disease known as Bell-miner","c":1,"x":0.13160539374450175},{"h":0.016235762687116906,"x":0.1316079454574908,"y":0.4228063401435147,"w":0.67712585449218754,"t":"Associated Die-back. The bell-miner is a bird, and the disease seems to be common where","c":1},{"w":0.68115453084309896,"h":0.015052260161850239,"t":"there are high populations of bell-miners. Again it's the leaves of the trees that are affected.","y":0.43734594851137831,"x":0.13163383423854147,"c":1},{"y":0.45267704776461803,"w":0.67499689737955726,"t":"What happens is that insects settle on the leaves and eat their way round them, destroying","x":0.13163570979319664,"h":0.014120323778743282,"c":1},{"t":"them as they go, and at the same time they secrete a solution which has sugar in it. The bell-","x":0.13158769526384115,"y":0.46553851483885511,"c":1,"h":0.017734317532416943,"w":0.691570078531901},{"y":0.48069860908374129,"w":0.68120763142903651,"h":0.015838577553577204,"c":1,"x":0.13162013621673377,"t":"miner birds really like this solution, and in order to get as much as possible, they keep away"},{"x":0.13161345936499194,"w":0.67711771647135421,"c":1,"t":"other creatures that might try to get it. So these birds and insects flourish at the expense of","h":0.014486615031571559,"y":0.49519788042565982},{"h":0.017375833154145925,"t":"other species, and eventually so much damage is done to the leaves that the tree dies.","x":0.1315871537453728,"y":0.50940361742901152,"w":0.64832977294921879,"c":1},{"t":"But experts say that trees can start looking sick before any sign of Bell-miner Associated Die-","y":0.55314284383476453,"w":0.69147730509440108,"h":0.015108675782615877,"c":1,"x":0.1336830766702182},{"w":0.68327006022135417,"c":1,"t":"back. So it looks as if the problem might have another explanation. One possibility is that it's","y":0.5675330293933879,"x":0.13367436102171865,"h":0.014852945599595269},{"x":0.13168724817617355,"t":"to do with the huge bushfires that we have in Australia. A theory proposed over 40 years ago","y":0.58274440525482407,"w":0.68724278767903635,"h":0.013250883392226132,"c":1},{"h":0.018078693933565648,"y":0.59568452872963673,"x":0.131566245004585,"t":"by ecologist William Jackson is that the frequency of bushfires in a particular region affects","w":0.67512486775716141,"c":1},{"h":0.01591806613935598,"y":0.61083295696062878,"w":0.67300084431966145,"t":"the type of vegetation that grows there. If there are very frequent bushfires in a region, this","x":0.13161563072723861,"c":1},{"t":"encourages grass to grow afterwards, while if the bushfires are rather less frequent, this","x":0.13365635319966676,"w":0.65243810017903647,"h":0.015785557642421066,"c":1,"y":0.62496487308728832},{"t":"results in the growth of eucalyptus forests.","x":0.13168724108061391,"h":0.011627907185728592,"y":0.64244186035207418,"w":0.31687243143717447,"c":1},{"x":0.13160549286042017,"t":"So why is this? Why do fairly frequent bushfires actually support the growth of eucalyptus?","y":0.66094711257243632,"h":0.017304005976700565,"c":1,"w":0.67507537841796883},{"t":"Well, one reason is that the fire stops the growth of other species which would consume","y":0.67623353484856985,"x":0.13163045514484339,"w":0.65446141560872395,"h":0.015787354908506246,"c":1},{"x":0.12956736799487117,"w":0.68325007120768233,"h":0.015994326947575077,"c":1,"y":0.69096046315484017,"t":"water needed by eucalyptus trees. And there's another reason. If these other quick-growing"},{"t":"species of bushes and plants are allowed to proliferate, they harm the eucalyptus in another","x":0.13374485315023388,"h":0.013081395583944722,"y":0.70639534871532395,"w":0.68518519083658858,"c":1},{"t":"way, by affecting the composition of the soil, and removing nutrients from it. So some","h":0.01652658617538616,"y":0.71867509452867828,"c":1,"x":0.13363997026418115,"w":0.62984415690104167},{"x":0.13367708849650001,"c":1,"w":0.64828745524088549,"t":"bushfires are actually essential for the eucalyptus to survive as long as they are not too","h":0.015160834129342438,"y":0.73395952823596344},{"w":0.68939132690429683,"x":0.13369892470958319,"h":0.014875486124530712,"y":0.74826947076650208,"c":1,"t":"frequent. In fact there's evidence that Australia's indigenous people practised regular burning"},{"t":"of bush land for thousands of years before the arrival of the Europeans.","x":0.13374485937489278,"h":0.013250883392226132,"w":0.53292180379231779,"c":1,"y":0.76442873987112236},{"h":0.015236926443866095,"c":1,"y":0.7840753908116217,"t":"But since Europeans arrived on the continent, the number of bushfires has been strictly","x":0.1336779460930422,"w":0.648297831217448},{"h":0.015589680351553836,"y":0.79863722320635122,"x":0.13366991878798226,"w":0.67505421956380207,"c":1,"t":"controlled. Now scientists believe that this reduced frequency of bushfires to low levels has"},{"h":0.014723203769140158,"x":0.13374484682846788,"c":1,"w":0.67078191121419273,"t":"led to what's known as 'dry rainforest', which seems an odd name as usually we associate","y":0.81389870419750499},{"x":0.1337448453134302,"y":0.82848837196491998,"t":"tropical rainforest with wet conditions. And what's special about this type of rainforest? Well,","w":0.68312759399414058,"c":1,"h":0.013089955625320671},{"x":0.13160101732252069,"y":0.84196801685590428,"c":1,"w":0.69359583536783853,"h":0.017506309617113303,"t":"unlike tropical rainforest which is a rich ecosystem, this type of ecosystem is usually a simple"},{"w":0.65444346110026042,"y":0.85692536189711921,"x":0.13368663907220765,"c":1,"h":0.015237103923891993,"t":"one. It has very thick, dense vegetation, but not much variety of species. The vegetation"},{"x":0.13568669446452683,"t":"provides lots of shade, so one species that does find it ideal is the bell-miner bird, which","w":0.65248672485351555,"h":0.017047067693883311,"c":1,"y":0.87043205186336459},{"t":"builds its nests in the undergrowth there. But again that's not helpful for the eucalyptus tree.","h":0.016807061904170362,"y":0.88563199887720867,"c":1,"w":0.68531244913736988,"x":0.1316246212825854},{"t":"100","w":0.03497942288716635,"y":0.91860465100676214,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.13374485635477074},{"x":0.85802469174571716,"c":1,"w":0.034979422887166378,"t":"Q31","y":0.15552325565279512,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"x":0.85802469175214735,"y":0.18459302311498449,"h":0.011627907185728703,"w":0.034979422887166378,"c":1,"t":"Q32"},{"c":1,"t":"Q33","w":0.037037035624186143,"x":0.85802469196842823,"h":0.013081395583944722,"y":0.32848837193186486},{"y":0.45203488356490185,"t":"Q34","w":0.034979422887166378,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"x":0.8600823049144416},{"t":"Q35","x":0.86008230492087134,"h":0.011627907185728592,"w":0.034979422887166378,"y":0.62499999985917054,"c":1},{"y":0.69040697658302763,"c":1,"x":0.86008230492815885,"w":0.034979422887166378,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"Q36"},{"c":1,"w":0.034979422887166378,"h":0.013081395583944611,"y":0.71947674402761341,"x":0.86008230492087134,"t":"Q37"},{"w":0.037811190287272201,"y":0.8116508222992953,"t":"Q38","x":0.86073422127245858,"c":1,"h":0.014923661841941827},{"y":0.84302325567312397,"x":0.86213991808959578,"t":"Q39","h":0.011627907185728703,"c":1,"w":0.034979422887166378},{"c":1,"t":"Q40","x":0.86213991809051438,"w":0.034979422887166267,"h":0.013081395583944722,"y":0.88517441844037814}]}